{"cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-251ed97c-ty2xvp", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "=== cloud-env-setup.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Rainbow (josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-): real Git LFS assets, Blender 5.3.0, Android SDK 34, World Labs plugin.\n# Every step is non-fatal so a session always starts. Copy: scripts/cloud-env-setup.sh\nif [ -d rainbow- ]; then\n  # A pull that failed once leaves \"access = basic\" in .git/config and every later pull then asks for a\n  # username (fails in a container). Clear it first; the session git proxy supplies the GitHub login.\n  (cd rainbow- && git config --unset-all \"lfs.https://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-.git/info/lfs.access\"; true)\n  (cd rainbow- && git lfs pull) || echo \"rainbow: git lfs pull failed (the SessionStart hook retries)\"\n  (cd rainbow- && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund > /dev/null 2>&1) || echo \"rainbow: npm ci failed\"\n  (cd rainbow- && bash scripts/setup-blender.sh) || echo \"rainbow: blender setup failed\"\n  (cd rainbow- && bash scripts/setup-android-sdk.sh) || echo \"rainbow: android sdk setup failed\"\n  (cd rainbow- && bash scripts/setup-worldlabs-plugin.sh) || echo \"rainbow: worldlabs plugin setup failed\"\nfi\nexit 0\n=== install-autosave-scheduler.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Installs (idempotently) the Rainbow five-minute autosave scheduler on this machine.\n#   * Linux with cron  -> crontab entry  */5 * * * *  + starts the cron daemon if it is not running\n#   * no cron available -> falls back to a detached loop daemon (scripts/autosave-daemon.sh)\n# Session env needed by git (proxy, CA bundle, url rewrites) is captured to ~/.rainbow-autosave.env\n# (chmod 600, outside the repo; it contains NO tokens — auth is handled by the git proxy/helper).\nset -u\nREPO=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nENVF=\"$HOME/.rainbow-autosave.env\"\nLOGD=\"$HOME/.rainbow-autosave\"\nmkdir -p \"$LOGD\"\n\n# 1. capture non-secret environment that git/curl need outside the interactive session\n{\n  echo \"# generated by install-autosave-scheduler.sh — proxy/CA/git-url settings only\"\n  for v in PATH HOME HTTPS_PROXY https_proxy HTTP_PROXY http_proxy NO_PROXY no_proxy SSL_CERT_FILE \\\n           CURL_CA_BUNDLE REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE GIT_SSL_CAINFO NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT \\\n           GIT_EDITOR GIT_CONFIG_COUNT; do\n    [ -n \"${!v-}\" ] && printf 'export %s=%q\\n' \"$v\" \"${!v}\"\n  done\n  n=\"${GIT_CONFIG_COUNT:-0}\"\n  for ((i=0; i<n; i++)); do\n    k=\"GIT_CONFIG_KEY_$i\"; val=\"GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_$i\"\n    printf 'export %s=%q\\n' \"$k\" \"${!k-}\"\n    printf 'export %s=%q\\n' \"$val\" \"${!val-}\"\n  done\n} > \"$ENVF\"\nchmod 600 \"$ENVF\"\n\nRUNNER=\"$REPO/scripts/autosave-cron.sh\"\nchmod +x \"$RUNNER\" \"$REPO/scripts/autosave-daemon.sh\" \"$REPO/scripts/rainbow-autosave.py\" 2>/dev/null\n\nif command -v crontab >/dev/null 2>&1 && command -v cron >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  LINE=\"*/5 * * * * $RUNNER cron >> $LOGD/cron.log 2>&1 # rainbow-autosave\"\n  ( crontab -l 2>/dev/null | grep -v '# rainbow-autosave' ; echo \"$LINE\" ) | crontab -\n  if ! pgrep -x cron >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    cron 2>/dev/null || /usr/sbin/cron 2>/dev/null || true\n  fi\n  if pgrep -x cron >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    echo \"scheduler=cron status=active entry='$LINE'\"\n    exit 0\n  fi\n  echo \"cron daemon could not start; falling back to loop daemon\" >&2\nfi\n\n# fallback: detached loop daemon with pidfile\nPIDF=\"$LOGD/daemon.pid\"\nif [ -f \"$PIDF\" ] && kill -0 \"$(cat \"$PIDF\")\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  echo \"scheduler=daemon status=active pid=$(cat \"$PIDF\")\"\n  exit 0\nfi\nsetsid nohup \"$REPO/scripts/autosave-daemon.sh\" >> \"$LOGD/daemon.log\" 2>&1 < /dev/null &\necho $! > \"$PIDF\"\necho \"scheduler=daemon status=started pid=$(cat \"$PIDF\")\"\n=== autosave-daemon.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Fallback scheduler used only when cron is unavailable: one autosave every 300 s.\nREPO